{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation detail for this story (the description carries the decisions). Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n**1. Tombstone registry (`src/rebar/_deprecations.py`) becomes exactly:**\n```\n_tomb(\"env\",\"TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR\",\"REBAR_TRACKER_DIR\",\"error\",removed_in=\"v0.8.0\")\n_tomb(\"env\",\"REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_RECONCILE_LIVE\",\"REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_JIRA_SYNC\",\"error\",removed_in=\"v0.8.0\")\n_tomb(\"cfg\",\"verify.require_verdict_for_close\",\"verify.require_completion_verification_for_close\",\"error\",removed_in=\"v0.8.0\")\n_tomb(\"file\",\".rebar/config.conf\",\"rebar.toml [tool.rebar]\",\"error\",removed_in=\"v0.8.0\")\n_tomb(\"env\",\"REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS\",\"REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS\",\"error\",removed_in=\"v0.8.0\")\n_tomb(\"env\",\"REBAR_LLM_MODEL\",\"the [tool.rebar.llm.model_classes] slots\",\"error\",removed_in=\"v0.12.0\")\n```\nEvidence for the releases: DE7 rows landed in 0.8.0 (`CHANGELOG.md:764-765`; commits `d2077673`/`7e29166a` are ancestors of `v0.8.0`, not of `v0.7.1`; `docs/release-notes.md:789,810-813`); `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` in 0.12.0 (`CHANGELOG.md:371-376`, `docs/release-notes.md:493`). The rows removed are the 7 warn env rows (`_deprecations.py:209-217`: `REBAR_PUSH`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_MAX_RETRIES`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_RETRY_BUDGET`, `REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ANALYZERS`, `REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ENABLED`, `REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_RESOLVED_STATUSES`) and the 6 warn cfg rows (`:226,227,231,236,240,241`: `reconciler.lock_backend`, `reconciler.lock_max_retries`, `code_health.analyzers`, `code_health.enabled`, `jira.resolved_statuses`, `reconciler.resolved_statuses`). The `show_config.py:182` f-string and `_tombstone_message` (`_deprecations.py:186-193`) need no template change; the `warn` branches (`show_config.py:180`, `_deprecations.py:193,280`) stay as vocabulary (`_TOMBSTONE_BEHAVIORS` is pinned by `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py:71`).\n\n**2. `_LLM_KNOWN_KEYS` (add in `src/rebar/_config_sections.py` next to `_RESERVED_SECTIONS`, `:209`):**\n```python\n_LLM_KNOWN_KEYS: tuple[str, ...] = (\"model\",\"model_provider\",\"base_url\",\"bedrock_region_name\",\n \"parse_failure_artifact_dir\",\"max_tokens\",\"max_steps\",\"timeout\",\"temperature\",\n \"llm_retry_max_attempts\",\"llm_retry_max_wait_s\",\"llm_tool_timeout_s\",\n \"mcp_servers\",\"headers\",\"model_classes\",\"evals\")\n```\nReads that define the 15 non-`evals` keys: `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py:152-158,180-206`, `src/rebar/llm/config.py:470,496`, `src/rebar/llm/headers.py:219`, `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:328`. `evals` is reserved for the eval-harness epic (which adds the `[llm.evals] corpus_root` reader in `llm/config_readers.py` and deletes the `{\"evals\"}` carve-out in the sync test).\n\n**3. Replace `_config_sections.py:223-224` with:**\n```python\nif sect in _RESERVED_SECTIONS:\n    if sect == \"llm\" and isinstance(val, dict):\n        _warn_unknown(\"llm\", {k: val[k] for k in val if k not in _LLM_KNOWN_KEYS}, source, strict=strict)\n    continue\n```\nMessage texts are the existing `_config_coercion.py:88` templates. Warn: `rebar config (<path>): unknown key 'llm.<key>' ignored (typo? see docs/config.md)`. Strict (`REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS=error`) raises: `rebar config (<path>): unknown key(s) llm.<key> (REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS=error — remove them or fix the typo)`.\n\n**4. Alias deletions, line by line:** `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:330-339` (`_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES` `:333`, `_map_legacy_env` `:336-339`); `src/rebar/config.py:9,45,56` (imports) and `:382-385` (the `_env_signature` alias loop); `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:32` (re-export); `src/rebar/_config_sections.py:196-198` (`_ALIASES`) and `:244-250` (consumer loop), `:243` becomes `warn_deprecated_cfg_keys(sect, d, logger=logger)`, `:22` `warn_deprecated` import dropped; `src/rebar/_commands/show_config.py:142-146`. `scripts/gen_env_registry.py:484-488`: comment cites `rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY`; attribution string `\"src/rebar/_deprecations.py (deprecation registry)\"` (no output change: REGISTRY has no env rows).\n\n**5. `docs/api-stability.md:27` replacement sentence:** \"Renames are communicated through the deprecation registry (`rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY`); the config/env alias-resolution tables were removed with the last alias (ADR 0116) and are re-introduced, with their removal window, by the first future rename that needs one.\" Keep `:30-34`.\n\n**6. `docs/config.md`:** `:862-902` \"Back-compat\" rewritten to state the unknown-key policy (default `warn`, unchanged — `_config_sources.py:357-363`), that `[llm]` now warns on unknown keys, and that there are no alias tables; `:886-902` replaced by the six error rows each naming its release, plus the sentence \"no warn-class tombstones remain: a removed inert config key is an ordinary unknown key; a removed inert env var is not read\". `:410-413`: change \"never warns on it\" to \"warns on an unknown `[tool.rebar.llm]` key exactly as for a core section\". `scripts/gen_config_reference.py:224-233,342-346`: add a `Removed in` column to `_cfg_tombstones`/the table, then `python scripts/gen_config_reference.py` regenerates `docs/config-reference.md`; `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py:255-267` additionally asserts `tomb.removed_in in row`. `tests/golden/config_surface.json` is unchanged (verified: none of the 13 names are in it); run `python scripts/generate_config_surface_golden.py --check`.\n\n**7. Test deletions, line by line:**\n- `tests/unit/test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py:98-99`\n- `tests/unit/test_config_show.py:38-39`\n- `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py:24` (import), `:52-54` (`accounted = _live_config_keys() | _tombstoned(\"cfg\")`), `:60` (`| _tombstoned(\"env\")`)\n- `tests/unit/test_config_backcompat.py:210-255` (the two code_health tombstone tests)\n- `tests/unit/test_config_resolved_statuses_removal.py:42-62,71-103` (tombstone rows/warn tests; keep `:35,64,105`)\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py:61` (`WARN_ENV`), `:96-97`, `:143-157`\n\n**8. Expected CLI strings (Testing section):**\n- `TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR=x rebar list` → non-zero; stderr `TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR was removed in v0.8.0 — use REBAR_TRACKER_DIR instead (migrate your config/env)`.\n- `TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR=x rebar config validate` → prints `ERROR: env TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR was removed in v0.8.0 — use REBAR_TRACKER_DIR instead`.\n- `rebar list` with `[llm] overlap_k = 5` → logs `rebar config (…/rebar.toml): unknown key 'llm.overlap_k' ignored (typo? see docs/config.md)`.\n- Interfaces test `test_error_env_var_fails_loud:124` asserts `removed_in in out`.\n\n**9. Release note text (`docs/release-notes.md` + `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`):** \"BREAKING (pre-1.0) — 13 warn-class tombstones retired. `REBAR_PUSH`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_MAX_RETRIES`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_RETRY_BUDGET`, `REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ANALYZERS`, `REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ENABLED`, `REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES`, `REBAR_RECONCILER_RESOLVED_STATUSES` are no longer read at all (no warning). `reconciler.lock_backend`, `reconciler.lock_max_retries`, `code_health.analyzers`, `code_health.enabled`, `jira.resolved_statuses`, `reconciler.resolved_statuses` are ordinary unknown keys: `rebar config (<file>): unknown key '<section>.<key>' ignored (typo? see docs/config.md)` (error under `REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS=error`). The six error-class tombstones now report the release they were removed in. Unknown `[tool.rebar.llm]` keys now warn like every other section.\""},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788807685492171785,"uuid":"455d83b9-8923-44ac-be7f-c1b9a7117c58"}